## 🔟 SCROLL VELOCITY-BASED TEXT EFFECT

### Problem
Text doesn't respond to scroll speed

### Solution: Blur/Scale on Scroll

```html
<h2 class="scroll-text" data-blur="true">
  Advanced Technology Solutions
</h2>

<style>
.scroll-text {
  font-size: 3rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  transition: filter 0.1s ease;
}

.scroll-text.blur {
  filter: blur(2px);
  opacity: 0.8;
}
</style>

<script>
const scrollTexts = document.querySelectorAll('[data-blur="true"]');
let lastScrollPos = 0;

window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
  const currentScrollPos = window.scrollY;
  const scrollVelocity = Math.abs(currentScrollPos - lastScrollPos);
  
  scrollTexts.forEach(text => {
    if (scrollVelocity > 5) {
      text.classList.add('blur');
    } else {
      text.classList.remove('blur');
    }
  });
  
  lastScrollPos = currentScrollPos;
});
</script>
